{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Observe.</b> Wait." "<b>The month of the Aviv.</b> The month of Nisan is called the month of the Aviv because the grain crops called aviv ripen in it — these are barley, as it is written: כי השעורה אביב." "<b>And you shall make Pesach.</b> He brought the verse back because of: you may not slaughter the Pesach. — In Aramaic, אהדריה קרא means 'he brought the verse back'; the specific derivation is not fully spelled out in the text." "<b>From Egypt, night.</b> The word night refers back to 'you shall make Pesach.' — Reading קאי אועשית as קאי א״ועשית, i.e., קאי על ועשית, 'refers to ועשית.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:52:59.539306103Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}